  "applies_to": "Eastron SDM120CTM single-phase CT-operated DIN-rail meter (1 A / 5 A CT secondary), protocol implementation V1.3. Not the SDM120CT-40mA.",
  "summary": "The SDM120CT-M is a single-phase DIN-rail kWh meter that measures through an external current transformer and reports over RS485 Modbus RTU. Readings are IEEE-754 floats in input register pairs (function 04). Holding registers set the CT primary and secondary, demand period, communication and pulse settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 2400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Registers are printed 30001/40001 style (six-digit 46xxxx for the F0xx/F9xx block) next to the hex start address sent on the wire, e.g. 30007 = 0x0006 and 463777 = 0xF920. Wire address = printed number minus 30001, 40001 or 400001."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Eastron SDM120CTM Smart Meter Modbus Protocol Implementation V1.3",
    "doc_number": "V1.3",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/fastron-electronics/image/upload/v1619064123/Eastron%20Europe/SDM120CT_Modbus_protocol.pdf",
    "pages": "Input and holding register tables, PDF pp. 5-8"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the document's read example returns 43 66 33 34 (high register first) for 230.2 V, so all floats here are ABCD.",
    "Floats must be read in register pairs starting on an even address; odd counts or starts return an exception.",
    "Left out: the serial number (464513), an unsigned 32-bit integer whose word order the document does not state, and the scroll-display time register (463745), whose format is given as BCD without an encoding rule.",
    "Source host: the PDF is served from the media store used by Eastron Europe (Fastron Electronics, Eastron's UK distributor) for its product pages.",
    "This is the 1 A / 5 A CT version; the SDM120CT-40mA has its own map in this library."
  ],
